  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.520 accuracy, far surpassing the image-only baseline (config_008, 0.332), confirming multimodal fusion is essential. The best config uses weighted fusion. Question: config_041 is a single-variable ablation of config_001, changing only the fusion strategy from weighted to concat while keeping scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, and transformer aggregation identical. This isolates whether concat fusion (which preserves full feature information before a learned downstream layer) outperforms weighted fusion (which commits to a fixed linear combination early). Why this is the best next experiment: Fusion strategy is a fundamental architectural decision that affects how complementary information from RNA and image modalities is combined. Resolving this question early (with 7 experiments remaining) will inform whether subsequent experiments should prioritize concat or weighted fusion, reducing the search space and allowing more targeted exploitation of the best-performing region."
